course: dictionary
lesson: 6086
title: Meteors and their three names
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A meteor is a streak of light in the night sky. People call it a shooting star, but it is not really a star. It is made when a small piece of rock or dust from space burns up in the air. «A meteor shot across the sky.»
explain: One piece of space rock can have three names, depending on where it is. In space it is a meteoroid. While it glows in the air it is a meteor. If any piece lands on the ground, it is a meteorite. «A space rock is a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air and a meteorite if a piece lands on the ground.»
explain: Use the context to choose the right name. Where is the rock? Is it glowing in the air? Has it landed? Ask these three questions and the right word becomes clear.
fact: A meteor is a streak of light in the sky, also called a shooting star.
fact: Most meteors glow and burn out between about 70 and 120 kilometres up, far above aeroplanes and clouds.
fact: A «meteor shower» means many meteors at once.
fact: Meteor showers happen when the Earth passes through trails of dust left by comets, such as the Perseids every August.
fact: The Perseids appear around 12 August, from comet Swift-Tuttle.
exercise: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid while it is in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» What is the name for the piece while it glows in the air? | Comet | Meteorite | Meteoroid | *Meteor
exercise: «A meteor shot across the sky.» What does a meteor look like in the sky? | *A streak of light | A big dark cloud | A piece of rock lying on the grass | A bright planet that never moves
exercise: What is a «meteor shower»? | *Many meteors at once | A star that never moves | A single rock that lands on the ground | A comet that burns in the day
test: «Most meteors glow and burn out between about 70 and 120 kilometres up.» Where do most meteors glow? | Under the sea | *Far above aeroplanes and clouds | Inside the Moon | Right on the ground
test: A meteoroid is in space, a meteor glows in the air, and a meteorite lands on the ground. Which name is for the piece after it has landed? | *Meteorite | Meteor | Comet | Meteoroid
exam: Which comet is the Perseids meteor shower linked to? | *Swift-Tuttle | The Sun | Mars | The Moon
